  "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8794893/",
  "notes": "Full recipe recovered from the primary literature: base medium 'MO (Missouri) medium' (Zane GM, Yen HB, Wall JD. 2010. Effect of the deletion of qmoABC and the promoter-distal gene encoding a hypothetical protein on sulfate reduction in Desulfovibrio vulgaris Hildenborough. Appl Environ Microbiol 76:5500-5509. PMID:20581180; DOI:10.1128/AEM.00691-10. Full verbatim recipe (modified from Zane et al. 2010) also given in Rajeev et al. 2020, Front Microbiol 11:610455, DOI:10.3389/fmicb.2020.610455 an",
  "verification": "paper-verified (recipe recovered from primary literature)",
  "verification_evidence": "Under respiratory conditions, 15 or 30 mM sodium lactate was added as the electron donor, and sodium sulfate (30 mM), sodium sulfite (10 or 20 mM) or sodium thiosulfate (10 or 20 mM) was added as the terminal electron acceptor.",
  "verification_confidence": "medium",
  "recipe_evidence": "Paper: 'D. vulgaris H WT and the two modified strains were grown anaerobically at 37 C in MO medium. Under respiratory conditions, 15 or 30 mM sodium lactate was added as the electron donor, and sodium sulfate (30 mM), sodium sulfite (10 or 20 mM) or sodium thiosulfate (10 or 20 mM) was added as the terminal electron acceptor.' Base MO medium (modified from Zane et al. 2010), verbatim from Rajeev et al. 2020: '8 mM magnesium chloride, 20 mM ammonium chloride, 0.6 mM calcium chloride, 2 mM phosphate buffer (pH 7.2), 30 mM Tris-HCl (pH 7.4)' plus '6 ml/L trace elements, 1 ml/L vitamin solution, ",
  "recipe_confidence": "high",
  "base_medium": "MO (Missouri) medium",
  "base_medium_reference": "Zane GM, Yen HB, Wall JD. 2010. Effect of the deletion of qmoABC and the promoter-distal gene encoding a hypothetical protein on sulfate reduction in Desulfovibrio vulgaris Hildenborough. Appl Environ Microbiol 76:5500-5509. PMID:20581180; DOI:10.1128/AEM.00691-10. Full verbatim recipe (modified from Zane et al. 2010) also given in Rajeev et al. 2020, Front Microbiol 11:610455, DOI:10.3389/fmicb.2020.610455 and in Fels et al. 2023, Front Microbiol 14:1095191 (PMC10102598). Vitamin solution per Brandis & Thauer 1981, J Gen Microbiol 126:249-252.",
